1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,300
Every equation you have solved so
far had an answer you could point to

2
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:05,563
on the number line.

3
00:00:05,963 --> 00:00:07,721
x minus three equals zero?

4
00:00:07,721 --> 00:00:08,843
Point at three.

5
00:00:08,843 --> 00:00:10,354
x squared equals four?

6
00:00:10,354 --> 00:00:12,311
Point at two, or minus two.

7
00:00:12,761 --> 00:00:15,614
Last night, Aarav met
one that broke the rule.

8
00:00:15,614 --> 00:00:17,456
A new chapter begins with it.

9
00:00:17,806 --> 00:00:19,958
x squared plus one equals zero.

10
00:00:19,958 --> 00:00:22,679
He tried every number he could think of.

11
00:00:22,679 --> 00:00:23,854
Not one worked.

12
00:00:24,354 --> 00:00:27,999
Is the equation broken, or
is the number line too small?

13
00:00:28,649 --> 00:00:30,554
So why does no number work?

14
00:00:30,904 --> 00:00:32,565
Three squared is nine.

15
00:00:32,565 --> 00:00:37,235
Minus three squared is also nine,
because minus times minus is plus.

16
00:00:37,635 --> 00:00:39,244
Zero squared is zero.

17
00:00:39,244 --> 00:00:41,449
So a square is never negative.

18
00:00:41,849 --> 00:00:43,928
Watch x slide along the line.

19
00:00:43,928 --> 00:00:46,210
x squared never drops below zero.

20
00:00:46,610 --> 00:00:49,698
So x squared plus one
is always at least one.

21
00:00:49,698 --> 00:00:51,441
It can never reach zero.

22
00:00:52,091 --> 00:00:56,714
Now draw the graph of y equals x
squared plus c, and let c change.

23
00:00:57,064 --> 00:01:00,349
Where the curve crosses
the x axis, y is zero.

24
00:01:00,349 --> 00:01:02,785
Those points are the real solutions.

25
00:01:03,185 --> 00:01:08,373
At c equal to minus four, the curve
cuts the axis at two and at minus two.

26
00:01:08,773 --> 00:01:09,954
Let c count up.

27
00:01:09,954 --> 00:01:12,896
The crossings move in,
to one and minus one.

28
00:01:13,296 --> 00:01:16,919
At c equal to zero, the
curve just touches the axis.

29
00:01:17,319 --> 00:01:19,238
Past zero, it lifts off.

30
00:01:19,238 --> 00:01:21,686
No crossing, so no real solution.

31
00:01:22,236 --> 00:01:27,445
At c equal to one, our equation, it
floats one full unit above the axis.

32
00:01:27,995 --> 00:01:29,777
Now prove it in four steps.

33
00:01:30,127 --> 00:01:31,027
Step one.

34
00:01:30,995 --> 00:01:33,993
Start with x squared plus one equals zero.

35
00:01:34,743 --> 00:01:35,643
Step two.

36
00:01:35,629 --> 00:01:37,789
Subtract one from both sides.

37
00:01:37,789 --> 00:01:39,841
x squared equals minus one.

38
00:01:40,591 --> 00:01:41,526
Step three.

39
00:01:41,526 --> 00:01:44,196
But every real square is zero or more.

40
00:01:44,946 --> 00:01:45,880
Step four.

41
00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:49,036
Nothing is zero or more
and also minus one.

42
00:01:49,036 --> 00:01:51,194
So no real number solves it.

43
00:01:51,944 --> 00:01:53,120
Side by side.

44
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:57,038
x squared minus one equals
zero crosses the axis twice.

45
00:01:57,438 --> 00:02:00,814
x squared plus one equals
zero never crosses.

46
00:02:00,814 --> 00:02:02,264
No real solution.

47
00:02:02,864 --> 00:02:03,955
Now you try.

48
00:02:03,955 --> 00:02:07,991
Does x squared plus four equals
zero have a real solution?

49
00:02:07,991 --> 00:02:09,347
Pause and decide.

50
00:02:12,547 --> 00:02:13,447
No!

51
00:02:13,004 --> 00:02:17,618
x squared is never negative, so x
squared plus four is at least four.

52
00:02:18,268 --> 00:02:20,583
Numbers have run out like this before.

53
00:02:20,933 --> 00:02:24,174
x plus five equals two
needs a negative number.

54
00:02:24,174 --> 00:02:26,724
Two x equals three needs a fraction.

55
00:02:27,124 --> 00:02:29,453
x squared equals two needs root two.

56
00:02:29,453 --> 00:02:31,726
Each time, the number system grew.

57
00:02:32,126 --> 00:02:35,192
Now x squared equals
minus one is stuck again.

58
00:02:35,842 --> 00:02:40,803
The Indian mathematicians Mahavira and
Bhaskara wrote that a negative number

59
00:02:40,803 --> 00:02:42,387
has no square root.

60
00:02:42,787 --> 00:02:47,552
In fifteen forty five, Cardan solved
a puzzle and got five plus root minus

61
00:02:47,552 --> 00:02:48,452
fifteen.

62
00:02:48,273 --> 00:02:50,407
He called such answers useless.

63
00:02:51,057 --> 00:02:54,368
So mathematicians grew the
number system once more.

64
00:02:54,718 --> 00:02:58,165
They named a new number, i,
whose square is minus one.

65
00:02:58,165 --> 00:03:01,106
In symbols, i is the
square root of minus one.

66
00:03:01,506 --> 00:03:03,186
Now x equals i works.

67
00:03:03,186 --> 00:03:07,249
i squared plus one is minus
one plus one, which is zero.

68
00:03:07,899 --> 00:03:08,927
Remember this.

69
00:03:08,927 --> 00:03:11,347
No real number has a negative square.

70
00:03:11,347 --> 00:03:14,132
That is why we need a new kind of number.

71
00:03:14,832 --> 00:03:16,296
But where does i live?

72
00:03:16,296 --> 00:03:17,804
Not on the number line.

73
00:03:18,154 --> 00:03:21,699
Multiplying by minus one
turns three into minus three.

74
00:03:21,699 --> 00:03:23,273
That is a half turn.

75
00:03:23,673 --> 00:03:25,640
i times i is minus one.

76
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:28,981
So multiplying by i
twice makes a half turn.

77
00:03:29,381 --> 00:03:32,385
Then multiplying by i
once is a quarter turn.

78
00:03:32,385 --> 00:03:34,313
Off the line, straight up.

79
00:03:34,963 --> 00:03:37,745
So complex numbers need
a second direction.

80
00:03:38,345 --> 00:03:39,245
Quick one.

81
00:03:39,235 --> 00:03:41,976
Start at three and multiply by i twice.

82
00:03:41,976 --> 00:03:43,398
Where do you land?

83
00:03:43,398 --> 00:03:44,656
Pause and think.

84
00:03:47,856 --> 00:03:48,839
Minus three!

85
00:03:48,839 --> 00:03:51,394
Two quarter turns make one half turn.

86
00:03:52,044 --> 00:03:53,780
Now, one worked example.

87
00:03:54,130 --> 00:03:59,143
Show x squared plus four x plus five
equals zero has no real solution.

88
00:03:59,143 --> 00:04:00,890
Then solve it with i.

89
00:04:01,390 --> 00:04:02,290
Step one.

90
00:04:02,282 --> 00:04:04,467
Write five as four plus one.

91
00:04:05,217 --> 00:04:06,117
Step two.

92
00:04:06,088 --> 00:04:09,740
That gives x plus two,
squared, equals minus one.

93
00:04:10,490 --> 00:04:11,437
Step three.

94
00:04:11,437 --> 00:04:13,763
A real square cannot be negative.

95
00:04:13,763 --> 00:04:15,883
So there is no real solution.

96
00:04:16,633 --> 00:04:17,684
Step four.

97
00:04:17,684 --> 00:04:20,945
With i, x plus two is i or minus i.

98
00:04:20,945 --> 00:04:23,952
So x is minus two plus or minus i.

99
00:04:24,702 --> 00:04:25,920
The graph agrees.

100
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:30,039
Its lowest point is at height
one, so it never touches the axis.

101
00:04:30,689 --> 00:04:32,155
Now, the exam trap.

102
00:04:32,505 --> 00:04:36,876
Many students say minus one
solves x squared equals minus one.

103
00:04:37,276 --> 00:04:41,876
But minus one, in brackets, squared,
is minus one times minus one.

104
00:04:41,876 --> 00:04:44,945
That is plus one, so it is not a solution.

105
00:04:45,595 --> 00:04:47,053
Where is this asked?

106
00:04:47,053 --> 00:04:48,265
Not on its own.

107
00:04:48,265 --> 00:04:52,637
It is the reason behind every complex
number question in this chapter.

108
00:04:53,237 --> 00:04:54,514
Exam level now.

109
00:04:54,514 --> 00:04:58,141
For how many integers c
is there no real solution?

110
00:04:58,141 --> 00:04:59,472
Pause and solve.

111
00:05:04,872 --> 00:05:06,369
The answer is C.

112
00:05:06,369 --> 00:05:07,269
Sixteen.

113
00:05:07,693 --> 00:05:09,052
Complete the square.

114
00:05:09,052 --> 00:05:11,931
x minus two, squared, equals four minus c.

115
00:05:12,431 --> 00:05:14,686
A real square is never negative.

116
00:05:14,686 --> 00:05:18,899
So there is no real solution
exactly when c is more than four.

117
00:05:19,399 --> 00:05:22,768
At c equal to four, x
equals two still works.

118
00:05:22,768 --> 00:05:25,800
So c is five to twenty: sixteen integers.

119
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:27,864
Here is your recap.

120
00:05:27,864 --> 00:05:29,368
Screenshot this card.

121
00:05:32,568 --> 00:05:35,405
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

122
00:05:35,805 --> 00:05:36,705
One.

123
00:05:36,357 --> 00:05:40,817
Why does x squared plus nine
equals zero have no real solution?

124
00:05:41,617 --> 00:05:42,517
Two.

125
00:05:42,123 --> 00:05:46,395
For which c does the graph of x
squared plus c miss the x axis?

126
00:05:47,195 --> 00:05:48,095
Three.

127
00:05:47,824 --> 00:05:51,847
Is minus one, in brackets,
squared, equal to minus one?

128
00:05:52,747 --> 00:05:55,586
Next time: what is i times i times i?

129
00:05:55,586 --> 00:05:58,799
And why do the powers
of i repeat every four?
